---

<BaseLayout
  title="Luxury Kitchen in Guataparo, Valencia | Step-by-Step Case Study | RemodelaT"
  description={project.excerpt}
  image={project.heroImage}
  activePage="projects"
>
  <!-- ============ EDITORIAL HERO ============ -->
  <header class="gu-hero">
    <img
      src={project.heroImage}
      alt="Finished luxury kitchen in a Guataparo quinta, Valencia: white base-cabinet line, backlit floating shelf and seamless epoxy floor"
      class="gu-hero-img"
      fetchpriority="high"
      loading="eager"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <div class="gu-hero-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="container gu-hero-content">
      <a href="/en/projects" class="gu-back">← Back to projects</a>
      <span class="gu-eyebrow">{project.kicker}</span>
      <h1>{project.title}</h1>
      <p class="gu-lead">{project.excerpt}</p>

      <dl class="gu-facts" aria-label="Project facts">
        {heroFacts.map((fact) => (
          <div class="gu-fact">
            <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
            <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>

      <div class="gu-hero-actions">
        <a href="#paso-a-paso" class="btn-premium btn-primary-premium">
          <span class="btn-content">See the step by step</span>
          <span class="btn-border"></span>
          <span class="btn-arrow">→</span>
        </a>
        <a href={whatsappHref} class="btn-premium btn-outline-premium" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span class="btn-content">Request assessment</span>
          <span class="btn-arrow">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============ STICKY QUICK NAVIGATION ============ -->
  <ProjectQuickNav
    items={quickNavItems}
    ctaHref={whatsappHref}
    ctaLabel="Request assessment"
    summary="Full kitchen relocation in a Guataparo quinta, documented phase by phase."
  />

  <!-- ============ BREADCRUMB ============ -->
  <nav class="gu-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <div class="container gu-breadcrumb-inner">
      <a href="/en">Home</a>
      <span class="gu-sep">/</span>
      <a href="/en/projects">Projects</a>
      <span class="gu-sep">/</span>
      <span class="gu-current">Luxury Kitchen in Guataparo</span>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- ============ 01 · OVERVIEW ============ -->
  <section class="section gu-summary" id="resumen">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="tag">In a nutshell</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">From closed compartment to the open heart of the quinta</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          This intervention went far beyond new finishes: the kitchen changed rooms,
          changed concept, and changed its relationship with the rest of the home.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gu-summary-grid">
        <article class="gu-summary-card">
          <span class="gu-summary-index">The challenge</span>
          <h3>Moving an entire kitchen without leaving a trace of the old one</h3>
          <p>
            The original kitchen was a closed compartment entered through a large double
            doorway. Relocating it involved far more than fitting new cabinets: the doorway
            had to be sealed, electrics and plumbing reinvented, the electric water heater
            removed and a floor built to unify the entire day zone.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="gu-summary-card">
          <span class="gu-summary-index">The solution</span>
          <h3>Blockwork, new utilities and a continuous white design</h3>
          <p>
            We sealed the doorway with 20 cm blockwork and a fine render, chased new utility
            routes through walls and floors, replaced the water heater with solar thermal
            panels and poured a jointless white epoxy floor. Over that canvas, a linear
            base-cabinet composition with a backlit floating shelf and Siemens appliances.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ 02 · FINAL RESULT ============ -->
  <section class="section gu-showcase" id="resultado">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="tag">Final result</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">First the destination — then the road</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Before explaining each phase, we show the result: so every step of the process
          is understood knowing where it led.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gu-showcase-grid">
        {resultadoShowcase.map((item, index) => (
          <figure
            class="gu-showcase-card"
            data-lightbox-item
            data-lightbox-group="guataparo-resultado"
            data-src={item.src}
            data-alt={item.alt}
            data-title={item.title}
            data-caption={item.caption}
            data-badge={item.badge}
          >
            <div class="gu-showcase-media">
              <img src={item.src} alt={item.alt} loading={index === 0 ? 'eager' : 'lazy'} decoding="async" />
              <span class="gu-media-chip" aria-hidden="true">Enlarge</span>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <span class="gu-showcase-badge">{item.badge}</span>
              <h3>{item.title}</h3>
              <p>{item.caption}</p>
              <button
                class="expand-photo-btn"
                type="button"
                data-lightbox-open
                data-group="guataparo-resultado"
                data-src={item.src}
              >View full size</button>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ 03 · STEP BY STEP (TIMELINE) ============ -->
  <section class="section gu-timeline-section" id="paso-a-paso">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="tag">The build, in order</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">The project step by step: six phases, zero improvisation</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Every phase is numbered and documented with the works executed and its real
          photography, so the journey reads as clearly as it was built.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="gu-timeline">
        {phases.map((phase, index) => (
          <article class:list={['gu-phase', index % 2 === 1 && 'gu-phase--alt']} id={`fase-${phase.number}`}>
            <div class="gu-phase-rail" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="gu-phase-dot"></span>
              <span class="gu-phase-number">{phase.number}</span>
            </div>

            <div class="gu-phase-body">
              <span class="gu-phase-kicker">{phase.kicker}</span>
              <h3>{phase.title}</h3>
              <p>{phase.body}</p>
              <ul class="gu-phase-checks">
                {phase.checks.map((check) => (
                  <li>{check}</li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>

            <figure
              class="gu-phase-media"
              data-lightbox-item
              data-lightbox-group="guataparo-pasos"
              data-src={phase.image.src}
              data-alt={phase.image.alt}
              data-title={phase.title}
              data-caption={phase.image.caption}
              data-badge={phase.kicker}
            >
              <div class="gu-phase-media-box">
                <img src={phase.image.src} alt={phase.image.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                <span class="gu-phase-media-badge">{phase.image.badge}</span>
                <span class="gu-media-chip" aria-hidden="true">Enlarge</span>
              </div>
              <figcaption>{phase.image.caption}</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ 04 · BEFORE / AFTER ============ -->
  <ProjectBeforeAfterSlider
    id="comparativa"
    eyebrow="Same zone, another life"
